{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1489392-list-of-splats-powers-by-games","id":1489392,"title":"List of splats/powers by games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-06T22:36:16-07:00","id":1489392,"title":"List of splats/powers by games?","content":"As someone who lacks pdf ownership ATM, but want some pre-knowledge beforehand, I correct in the following?:<br /> <br /> Paramorphs are powered by Flux, the energy between possibilities. They are called Talents by default, were called Daredevils in Adventure!, and Assassins are a specialized variant of them.<br /> <br /> Psychomorphs are powered by Psi, the energy of emergent noospheric/noetic phenomena. Naturally occurring ones are called Psiads, artificially awakened ones are called Psions (and the functional difference is\u2026?). They were called Mesmerists in Adventure!.<br /> <br /> Eximorphs are powered by Quantum, the energy governing physical phenomena. They were called Novas in Aberrant, are called Aberrants in \u00c6eon, and were called Stalwarts in Adventure!.<br /> <br /> The most recent game, \u00c6ther, has Squires, Gog, and Magogs, all powered by Aether.<br /> <br /> Anything I mistook or missed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c